    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nNone\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nI developed some times ago a [simple plugin](https://github.com/dpretet/vim-leader-mapper) to create a menu for leader key mapping, like present in Spacemacs. I tried Spacemacs and I found their menu is awesome. \r\n\r\nI just ported my Neovim setup to use a Lua-based init file and I'm considering porting my plugin in Lua. Would you be interested to add it in your mini collection? My plugin is easy to configure from [a vim script or Lua dictionary](https://github.com/dpretet/dotfiles/blob/master/nvim/init.lua#L264) and bind any regular command or function call. The plugin doesn't have code dependency.\r\n\r\nBTW, thanks for your work, I love your plugins :)\r\n\r\nDamien\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1440\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2131563/209434204-a4a11c0d-5899-480e-ad56-b50434864edb.png\">\r\n",
